\details{
Port Commercial Fishing Activity Indicators are a suite of indicators used to understand relative participation rates of commercial fishing ports over time. They are comprised of commercial fishing landings and permit data from 2010 through 2025 summarized to indicate port-level activity in commercial fishing.

The PCFA analysis is conducted for across the Greater Atlantic Region (MA and NE) such that scores are comparable across both sub-regions. Note, the Mid-Atlantic analysis for the PCFA Indicator does not include data from North Carolina (NC) given the incompatibility of data from the Southeast. In particular, landings information in the Southeast is not assigned to the location of landing, but to the dealer address. NC ports land a significant portion of fish from Southeast managed species and thus, we elected to not include NC to avoid the risk of underestimation.
